y><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan-Taliban conflict: How India could benefit from shifting regional dynamics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a44371974eaa50194551865309a78403d2d7566a61ec74185f536a3b45bc3fc1</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426--f7ab516276cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Pakistan's influence in Afghanistan comes under strain, India is rebuilding ties with the Taliban in Kabul. Can New Delhi turn this diplomatic opening into lasting strategic gains?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: India-US trade deal 'pretty close,' says Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84875e7224a725a5bbfdeff856650df997cc28c598c938a58a3fa60856f7d26c</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-us-trade-deal-pretty-close-says-trump/live-79719383--cfe288ad80da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-india-us-trade-deal-pretty-close-says-trump/live-79719383?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump hinted that the US-India trade deal could look different from the previous ones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korean workers treated as 'slaves' at Russian drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb241807f107024ba74b3825f2aa8948b0e8328bc317d645f513c3383d45ef0b</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877--83771c04f78a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-workers-treated-as-slaves-at-russian-drone-factory/a-79710877?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report reveals the plight of North Korean workers at a drone factory in Russia. It also raised concerns that Pyongyang could gain hands-on knowledge of advanced weapons systems through the workers it sends there.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the women powering India's youth-led 'Cockroach' protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6a9c40dd754703cd229bef7547028e2825ba7893d4758eaa415a4ea4bd45cd7</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824--e78a361757e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-are-the-women-powering-india-s-youth-led-cockroach-protests/a-79709824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing online harassment and police detentions, women are taking to the streets of Indian cities in large numbers for the youth-led "Cockroach" protests. Amid a large-scale crackdown, they refuse to be seen as victims.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a6a61174d241e9be2370cee6bcba64de1ea54653965ea96e3c4c51802b9b54</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f5fd316c9435e792a015903c08688e39ead8b329e23ca575e4ef277dcc70625</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The murder of a young mother in Iran has once again sparked debate on femicide and the social acceptance of violence against women.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3395a6f7ae2eb314e43f152300bd809e9220b47361399978557772fa4a1da7b3</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-accept/a-79681977--0dbaaaebbc74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-murder-of-a-young-mother-in-iran-has-once-again-sparked-debate-on-femicide-and-the-social-acceptance-of-violence-against-women/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-22T13:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
